# sshd configuration for the opt-in SFTP/SSH bench.
#
# This is a template: every @BENCH_RUN@ placeholder is a directory
# `just bench-up` substitutes with an absolute path (bench/run/sshd)
# before starting sshd. `just bench-up` generates a fresh host key
# into that directory (never a real system host key) and an
# `authorized_keys` file from a bench-only key pair it also generates,
# so this daemon never touches real user accounts or real SSH trust.
#
# Port 2222 needs no privilege to bind, so this daemon runs as the
# same unprivileged user as every other bench daemon.
#
# No SFTP bench test lives in this file's owning task (`bench_mounts.rs`
# covers SMB, NFS, and implicit FTPS only); this config exists so
# `just bench-up`'s sshd step has something to start, ready for an
# SFTP bench added later. See docs/TESTING.md.

Port 2222
ListenAddress 127.0.0.1
Protocol 2
HostKey @BENCH_RUN@/ssh_host_ed25519_key

PidFile @BENCH_RUN@/sshd.pid
LogLevel ERROR

PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AuthorizedKeysFile @BENCH_RUN@/authorized_keys
PermitRootLogin no
StrictModes no
UsePAM no
Subsystem sftp internal-sftp

# Bench connections use whichever account starts sshd; this only
# narrows what that account's session can do once authenticated, not
# who can authenticate.
X11Forwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
